{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013t7kjGzYBXkQo22zeiW3U7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for the \"worst\" tier scenario for each planned experiment in their experiment plan. Let me carefully think through what each experiment would yield under the worst-case scenario where the treatment's advantage over baseline disappears on clean data, indicating the current performance gap is primarily due to lexical/label confounds.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment:\n\n**plan_001: data_quality_fix**\n- In worst case, TF-IDF drops but barely — maybe to 0.70-0.74 range, requiring multiple rounds of normalization. This shows original separation was heavily lexical.\n\n\n**plan_002: core_revalidation_clean**\n- Under worst-case conditions, the treatment and baseline converge completely on clean data, with the 5-point gap vanishing entirely and both approaches performing at parity.\n**plan_003: scrambled_label_ablation**\n- Scrambling the persuasion labels produces minimal degradation (under 4 points), suggesting the labels themselves provide little meaningful signal to the model.\n**plan_004: adversarial_perturbation**\n- Both approaches degrade at similar rates under adversarial perturbation, so the relative performance gap doesn't change meaningfully.\n**plan_005: multi_attack_generation**\n- This is a data generation task rather than a hypothesis test, so it should succeed regardless of the tier outcome.\n**plan_006: cross**\n- The treatment fails to generalize better than the baseline when evaluated against novel attack types.\n**plan_007: tfidf_lr_baseline**\n- Even with normalization applied, TF-IDF and logistic regression still capture enough lexical patterns to perform reasonably well on clean data.\n**plan_008: strategy_transition_analysis**\n- The transition matrices show too much noise to clearly identify the monotonic escalation pattern I was looking for.\n**plan_009: wildchat_hard_negatives**\n- Both approaches struggle with false positives on the hard negatives from WildChat.\n**plan_010: cross_checkpoint_variance**\n- Performance fluctuates significantly across different checkpoints, indicating the model isn't stable.\n**plan_011: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction**\n- The DeepContext proxy performs just as well as the treatment, which suggests that grounding in persuasion techniques doesn't actually provide an advantage.\n\nNow I'm compiling the detailed YAML with specific numbers...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11584,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11584},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"911fde5c-4c95-4d22-bdca-28c03087a7ad","uuid":"eb47e831-8658-4e0f-8a28-2ef05882345e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013t7kjGzYBXkQo22zeiW3U7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心detection优势不成立，需要完全reframe。推荐方向(1)方法论贡献型——将TF-IDF=1.0发现本身及register-normalization\n  protocol作为核心贡献，论证现有multi-turn detection工作系统性高估检测能力。Paper type从\"new method\"\n  转向\"analysis/evaluation methodology\"，仍冲EMNLP main但投methodology track。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: data_quality_fix\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: \"Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling,验证TF-IDF降到<0.75\"\n    expected_results:\n      tfidf_before_normalization: 1.0\n      tfidf_after_first_pass: 0.82\n      tfidf_after_second_pass: 0.73\n      normalization_rounds_needed: 2\n      label_fix_applied: true\n      benign_strategy_class: \"none_class_9\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      TF-IDF需要两轮normalization才降到阈值以下（0.73），说明原始数据中jailbreak和benign的register差异\n      极大——攻击对话使用了明显不同于benign的词汇分布（更formal/technical的register、特定prompt模板词汇）。\n      第一轮paraphrase仅消除表层模板词但保留了domain-specific术语差异，需要第二轮targeted normalization\n      才勉强达标。这本身就是一个强信号：原始pilot phase_b的perfect F1=1.0主要来自lexical shortcut。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"TF-IDF Separation After Each Normalization Round\"\n        rows:\n          - [raw_data, 1.0, \"Perfect lexical separation\"]\n          - [round_1_paraphrase, 0.82, \"Template words removed, register gap remains\"]\n          - [round_2_targeted, 0.73, \"Barely passes gate after domain term normalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"TF-IDF feature importance heatmap showing top-50 discriminative tokens before/after normalization — before: dominated by prompt template tokens and register markers; after: residual separation from topic words not fully removable without destroying content\"\n    analysis: >\n      HARD GATE通过但仅勉强（0.73 vs 阈值0.75）。两轮normalization的必要性本身是方法论贡献的核心evidence：\n      它证明multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmark中存在系统性lexical confound。在reframe方向(1)下，\n      这个实验的finding从\"obstacle to overcome\"变为\"primary contribution\"。\n\n  - name: core_revalidation_clean\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: \"在clean data上重新训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.68\n      baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.66\n      treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.72\n      baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.70\n      treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n      baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.76\n      treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.83\n      baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.82\n      treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.86\n      baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.85\n      delta_k2_pp: 2\n      delta_k3_pp: 2\n      delta_full_pp: 1\n      deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.63\n    result_rationale: >\n      去除lexical confound后，treatment与baseline的差距从原始的10+pp收缩到1-2pp（不显著）。\n      核心原因：DeBERTa persuasion分类器在clean data上accuracy从0.7963降到0.63——8-class taxonomy\n      过于fine-grained，在register-normalized data上许多strategy boundary变得模糊（e.g., \"authority appeal\"\n      vs \"logical appeal\"在paraphrase后难以区分）。由于persuasion encoder本身quality下降，其生成的\n      embeddings不再携带比vanilla DeBERTa显著更多的信息。Baseline的vanilla DeBERTa embeddings在clean\n      data上反而更稳定，因为它不依赖于noisy strategy labels。2pp的delta在72-sample test set上\n      bootstrap CI完全overlap，p>0.3。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"F1 Comparison: Treatment vs Baseline on Clean Data (N=72 test)\"\n        rows:\n          - [K=1, 0.68, 0.66, \"+2pp\", \"p=0.41\"]\n          - [K=2, 0.72, 0.70, \"+2pp\", \"p=0.35\"]\n          - [K=3, 0.78, 0.76, \"+2pp\", \"p=0.32\"]\n          - [K=5, 0.83, 0.82, \"+1pp\", \"p=0.58\"]\n          - [Full, 0.86, 0.85, \"+1pp\", \"p=0.62\"]\n      - caption: \"DeBERTa Encoder Quality: Original vs Clean Data\"\n        rows:\n          - [persuasion_acc_original, 0.7963]\n          - [persuasion_acc_clean, 0.63]\n          - [intent_acc_original, 0.9514]\n          - [intent_acc_clean, 0.88]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bootstrap confidence interval plot for delta(treatment-baseline) at each K — all CIs cross zero\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix for 8-class persuasion classifier on clean data showing heavy off-diagonal mass between adjacent strategies\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta_k2=2pp < required 5pp，且统计不显著。Persuasion grounding在去除\n      lexical shortcut后不提供有意义增量。DeBERTa学到的主要是intent分类信号（acc仍0.88）而非persuasion\n      strategy信号（acc降至0.63）。这意味着Claim 2（early detection via persuasion grounding）在当前\n      数据/taxonomy下不成立。但这个negative result本身有价值：它说明仅fine-tune on persuasion labels\n      不足以在clean setting下获得detection优势，可能需要更大规模的persuasion标注数据或更粗粒度的taxonomy。\n\n  - name: scrambled_label_ablation\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: \"随机打乱persuasion strategy labels重新训练，对比properly-labeled treatment\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_proper_k2_f1: 0.72\n      treatment_scrambled_k2_f1: 0.70\n      treatment_proper_full_f1: 0.86\n      treatment_scrambled_full_f1: 0.84\n      scrambled_label_drop_k2_pp: 2\n      scrambled_label_drop_full_pp: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scrambled labels仅导致2pp下降（<4pp阈值），说明persuasion labels本身不是关键信号源。\n      原因：在clean data上DeBERTa persuasion分类器本身就只有0.63 accuracy，意味着encoder学到的\n      representation中persuasion strategy信息就不强。Scrambled labels让encoder无法学到coherent\n      strategy patterns，但由于原始labels在clean data上本就noisy（8类之间boundary模糊），\n      scrambling的marginal damage有限。真正驱动detection的是GRU从conversation-level temporal\n      patterns中学到的信号（turn数、response长度变化等meta-features），这些不依赖于strategy labels\n      的correctness。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Scrambled Label Ablation Results\"\n        rows:\n          - [K=2, 0.72, 0.70, \"-2pp\"]\n          - [K=3, 0.78, 0.76, \"-2pp\"]\n          - [Full, 0.86, 0.84, \"-2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: proper vs scrambled label performance across K values — gaps uniformly small and within CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      结论：persuasion strategy labels在clean data regime下不carry significant signal beyond acting\n      as a noisy regularizer。这支持worst-tier核心假设——当前taxonomy粒度（8 classes）在480-sample\n      regime下无法学到robust strategy representations。对reframe方向的implication：不能claim\n      \"persuasion labels are the key ingredient\"，但可以claim \"current taxonomy granularity is\n      insufficient\"作为future work direction。\n\n  - name: adversarial_perturbation\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: \"对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment vs baseline degradation\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_f1_before_perturbation: 0.86\n      treatment_f1_after_perturbation: 0.71\n      baseline_f1_before_perturbation: 0.85\n      baseline_f1_after_perturbation: 0.72\n      treatment_drop_pp: 15\n      baseline_drop_pp: 13\n      delta_delta_pp: -2\n      tfidf_f1_after_perturbation: 0.58\n      tfidf_drop_pp: 15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Treatment和baseline在perturbation下同步下降约14-15pp，delta-delta为-2pp（不显著且方向错误）。\n      核心原因：adversarial paraphrasing不仅消除lexical cues（TF-IDF baseline崩溃到0.58），也破坏了\n      DeBERTa encoder（无论persuasion-grounded还是vanilla）所依赖的surface-level linguistic patterns。\n      Persuasion-grounded encoder理论上应capture deeper pragmatic structure，但由于其persuasion\n      classification本身就在clean data上只有0.63 accuracy，它学到的representation并不比vanilla encoder\n      更\"pragmatic\"——两者都主要依赖sentence-level semantic features而非genuine illocutionary act\n      encoding。Aggressive paraphrasing保留了propositional content但改变了sentence structure，\n      两种encoder的degradation profile因此相似。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Adversarial Perturbation Results (Full Conversation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [Treatment, 0.86, 0.71, \"-15pp\"]\n          - [Baseline, 0.85, 0.72, \"-13pp\"]\n          - [TF-IDF+LR, 0.73, 0.58, \"-15pp\"]\n      - caption: \"Delta-Delta Analysis\"\n        rows:\n          - [treatment_drop, -15]\n          - [baseline_drop, -13]\n          - [delta_delta, -2, \"wrong direction, n.s.\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Degradation waterfall chart showing parallel decline for treatment and baseline under perturbation levels (light/moderate/aggressive)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-conversation F1 change under perturbation, treatment vs baseline — points clustered around diagonal (no systematic advantage)\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta-delta=-2pp，方向错误且不显著（需要>3pp正向）。Claim 1（Pragmatic\n      Evasion Asymmetry）在empirical层面不成立——persuasion-grounded features并不比semantic features\n      更robust to perturbation。这是worst tier最致命的finding：理论上最elegant的claim（pragmatic\n      patterns structurally harder to evade）没有empirical support。TF-IDF baseline的崩溃（-15pp）\n      确认perturbation有效消除了lexical cues，但treatment未能展现预期的robustness优势。\n\n  - name: multi_attack_generation\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: \"生成FITD和Deceptive Delight两种额外攻击类型的对话数据\"\n    expected_results:\n      fitd_conversations_generated: 65\n      deceptive_delight_conversations_generated: 58\n      fitd_avg_turns: 6.2\n      dd_avg_turns: 4.8\n      fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.92\n      dd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.89\n      generation_quality_pass_rate: 0.78\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据生成本身不受tier影响——这是pipeline execution而非hypothesis testing。Qwen3-8B成功生成\n      足够数量的对话，strategy annotation coverage >85%。但generation_quality_pass_rate（0.78）\n      略低于ideal，部分生成的对话persuasion structure不够naturalistic（特别是Deceptive Delight\n      的interleaving pattern对LLM来说较难faithful reproduce）。这些数据将在plan_006的cross-attack\n      evaluation中暴露问题。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Generated Attack Data Summary\"\n        rows:\n          - [FITD, 65, 6.2, 0.92, 0.81]\n          - [Deceptive_Delight, 58, 4.8, 0.89, 0.74]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strategy distribution comparison across three attack types (Crescendo vs FITD vs Deceptive Delight) — shows different strategy emphasis patterns\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据生成成功满足pass criteria（>=50 per type）。但在worst tier context下，这些数据的价值\n      从\"generalization evidence for our method\"变为\"additional test cases revealing method limitations\"\n      或\"attack diversity evidence for methodology paper\"。\n\n  - name: cross_attack_evaluation\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: \"在FITD和Deceptive Delight上zero-shot评估Crescendo-trained模型\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_fitd_f1: 0.58\n      baseline_fitd_f1: 0.56\n      treatment_dd_f1: 0.54\n      baseline_dd_f1: 0.52\n      cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg: 0.56\n      cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg: 0.54\n      cross_attack_delta_pp: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      两者都在unseen attack types上大幅下降（从0.85-0.86降到0.54-0.58），且treatment对baseline的\n      优势仅2pp（不显著）。根本原因：如果persuasion grounding真的capture了attack-agnostic的pragmatic\n      escalation pattern，treatment应在cross-attack setting下展现更强泛化能力（因为不同attack types\n      共享底层persuasion playbook）。但由于encoder学到的主要是Crescendo-specific的surface patterns\n      而非genuine pragmatic structure，cross-attack泛化能力与vanilla baseline无异。两者的low absolute\n      performance（0.54-0.58）说明Crescendo-specific training signal（无论lexical还是semantic）\n      都不transfer well，这在worst tier下是预期内的——没有genuine pragmatic feature的robustness\n      保证，模型就是在overfit to training distribution。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - [FITD, 0.58, 0.56, \"+2pp\", \"n.s.\"]\n          - [Deceptive_Delight, 0.54, 0.52, \"+2pp\", \"n.s.\"]\n          - [Average, 0.56, 0.54, \"+2pp\", \"n.s.\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: in-domain (Crescendo) vs cross-attack (FITD, DD) performance for treatment and baseline — both collapse similarly on OOD data\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS。但对reframe方向(1)有正面意义：cross-attack failure + in-domain dependence\n      on lexical cues共同论证了\"现有multi-turn detection方法泛化能力被高估\"的thesis。可作为\n      methodology paper中illustrating the problem的evidence。\n\n  - name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: \"Clean data上的TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      clean_tfidf_lr_f1: 0.70\n      clean_tfidf_lr_precision: 0.72\n      clean_tfidf_lr_recall: 0.68\n      tfidf_feature_count_above_threshold: 47\n    result_rationale: >\n      即使在register-normalized data上（TF-IDF separation从1.0降到0.73），TF-IDF+LR仍能达到\n      F1=0.70。这说明两轮normalization虽然消除了most obvious的register markers，但仍有residual\n      lexical signal（47个features仍有discriminative power）。这意味着即使我们的\"clean data\"\n      仍然不完全clean——topic-level词汇差异（jailbreak conversations inevitably discuss different\n      topics than benign ones）是无法完全消除的confound without destroying content validity。\n      这是methodology paper的核心argument之一：lexical confound在multi-turn detection中是\n      structural的，不仅仅是data hygiene问题。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"TF-IDF+LR on Clean Data\"\n        rows:\n          - [F1, 0.70]\n          - [Precision, 0.72]\n          - [Recall, 0.68]\n          - [Discriminative_features, 47]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Top-20 TF-IDF features after normalization with weights — showing residual topic-level rather than register-level discrimination\"\n    analysis: >\n      TF-IDF+LR的0.70 F1与neural models（treatment 0.86, baseline 0.85）之间的gap说明neural models\n      确实学到了beyond-lexical的signal。但treatment vs baseline的1pp gap说明这个beyond-lexical signal\n      不是来自persuasion grounding，而是来自generic sentence semantics。对evasion hierarchy narrative\n      的implication：lexical(0.70) < semantic(0.85) ≈ pragmatic(0.86)——hierarchy的后两层collapse了。\n\n  - name: strategy_transition_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: \"计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices并可视化\"\n    expected_results:\n      jailbreak_monotonicity_score: 0.52\n      benign_monotonicity_score: 0.45\n      monotonicity_gap: 0.07\n      transition_entropy_jailbreak: 2.1\n      transition_entropy_benign: 2.3\n      clear_escalation_visible: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Jailbreak对话的monotonicity score（0.52）仅略高于benign（0.45），差距不足以支撑\"monotonic\n      escalation trajectory\"的claim。原因有二：(1) DeBERTa persuasion classifier在clean data上\n      accuracy=0.63意味着strategy labels本身就noisy，computed transitions基于noisy labels自然\n      pattern不清晰；(2) Register normalization改变了句子的surface form，部分breaks了persuasion\n      classifier学到的pattern（它在original register上train的），导致strategy assignment在\n      normalized data上更random。Transition entropy差异也很小（2.1 vs 2.3），说明jailbreak对话\n      并没有显著更deterministic的strategy progression。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Trajectory Statistics: Jailbreak vs Benign\"\n        rows:\n          - [monotonicity_score, 0.52, 0.45, \"Δ=0.07\"]\n          - [transition_entropy, 2.1, 2.3, \"Δ=0.2\"]\n          - [dominant_path_frequency, 0.18, 0.14, \"Δ=0.04\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strategy transition heatmap (jailbreak) — diffuse pattern without clear dominant path, most cells have non-trivial probability mass\"\n      - \"Strategy transition heatmap (benign) — similar diffuse pattern, not clearly more 'oscillatory' than jailbreak\"\n      - \"2D PCA trajectory plot — jailbreak and benign trajectories heavily overlap, no clear separation in strategy space\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 3（Monotonic Escalation Trajectory）在clean data + noisy classifier regime下不成立。\n      这排除了reframe方向(2)（分析贡献型依赖trajectory可视化成立）。剩余可行方向：(1)方法论贡献型\n      或(3)negative result型。如果figures经过careful curation能找到个别illustrative examples\n      showing escalation pattern，可以作为qualitative observation保留，但不能作为quantitative claim。\n\n  - name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: \"从WildChat筛选high-drift benign对话作为hard negatives评估FPR\"\n    expected_results:\n      wildchat_filtered_conversations: 120\n      contamination_rate_before_filter: 0.15\n      contamination_rate_after_filter: 0.03\n      treatment_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.22\n      baseline_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.20\n      treatment_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.08\n      baseline_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      Treatment在hard negatives上的FPR（0.22）与baseline（0.20）相当，且都超过15%阈值。\n      High-drift benign对话（e.g., 从casual聊天转向technical discussion的对话）会触发false\n      positives，因为模型（无论treatment还是baseline）将conversation-level semantic drift\n      误判为adversarial escalation。Persuasion grounding理论上应区分\"genuine topic drift\"\n      和\"adversarial strategy escalation\"，但由于classifier accuracy不足（0.63），这种区分\n      能力没有materialized。FPR=0.22在实际deployment中unacceptable。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives\"\n        rows:\n          - [Treatment_hard, 0.22, \"FAILS <15% threshold\"]\n          - [Baseline_hard, 0.20, \"FAILS <15% threshold\"]\n          - [Treatment_easy, 0.08, \"passes\"]\n          - [Baseline_easy, 0.09, \"passes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"FPR distribution across conversation drift levels — monotonically increasing for both models, treatment offers no advantage in high-drift regime\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS（FPR=0.22 > 15%阈值）。在reframe context下，这进一步支持\"current\n      approaches conflate conversational drift with adversarial escalation\"的methodology critique。\n\n  - name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: \"评估多个DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoint的下游performance variance\"\n    expected_results:\n      epoch2_full_f1: 0.84\n      epoch3_full_f1: 0.86\n      epoch_final_full_f1: 0.85\n      variance_across_checkpoints_pp: 2\n      epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.59\n      epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.63\n      epoch_final_persuasion_acc: 0.62\n    result_rationale: >\n      Variance=2pp刚好在pass criteria边界上。但更关键的observation是：downstream detection\n      performance（0.84-0.86）与persuasion accuracy（0.59-0.63）之间的correlation很弱——\n      epoch2的persuasion acc最低（0.59）但detection F1仅比best低2pp。这进一步confirming\n      scrambled label ablation的conclusion：persuasion classification quality对detection\n      performance的contribution minimal。GRU主要在学conversation-level statistical patterns\n      而非strategy-level semantic patterns。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-Checkpoint Evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - [Epoch_2, 0.59, 0.84]\n          - [Epoch_3, 0.63, 0.86]\n          - [Epoch_final, 0.62, 0.85]\n          - [Variance, \"—\", \"2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: persuasion classification accuracy vs downstream detection F1 across checkpoints — weak/no correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pass criteria marginally met（variance=2pp），但secondary finding（weak correlation between\n      encoder quality and detection performance）是worst tier的additional evidence。\n\n  - name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: \"BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline复现DeepContext-like方法\"\n    expected_results:\n      proxy_full_f1: 0.83\n      proxy_k2_f1: 0.69\n      proxy_k3_f1: 0.75\n      treatment_full_f1: 0.86\n      treatment_k2_f1: 0.72\n      delta_vs_proxy_full_pp: 3\n      delta_vs_proxy_k2_pp: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      DeepContext proxy（BERT-base + GRU）在clean data上达到F1=0.83，与treatment（0.86）仅差3pp。\n      考虑到BERT-base vs DeBERTa-v3-base本身的capacity差异（DeBERTa在NLU benchmarks上typically\n      优于BERT 2-4pp），这3pp的gap可能entirely attributable to encoder capacity而非persuasion\n      grounding的contribution。这意味着：将DeBERTa换成BERT并去掉persuasion fine-tuning，\n      performance下降幅度与expected encoder capacity difference一致——persuasion grounding的\n      incremental contribution statistically indistinguishable from zero。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"DeepContext Proxy vs Treatment\"\n        rows:\n          - [K=2, 0.69, 0.72, \"+3pp (encoder capacity?)\"]\n          - [K=3, 0.75, 0.78, \"+3pp\"]\n          - [Full, 0.83, 0.86, \"+3pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Performance comparison bar chart: BERT-base+GRU vs vanilla-DeBERTa+GRU vs persuasion-DeBERTa+GRU — showing consistent ~1-3pp gaps that track encoder capacity not persuasion grounding\"\n    analysis: >\n      Confound：DeBERTa > BERT的gap（~3pp）与persuasion grounding的claimed contribution（~1-2pp\n      over vanilla DeBERTa）叠加后，无法cleanly attribute任何portion到persuasion specifically。\n      对methodology paper有价值：shows that encoder choice matters more than fine-tuning objective，\n      further undermining the pragmatic grounding hypothesis。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11584,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11584},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"911fde5c-4c95-4d22-bdca-28c03087a7ad","uuid":"a37776bf-7b01-41b5-ad38-d726465ff79f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":156081,"duration_api_ms":157399,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心detection优势不成立，需要完全reframe。推荐方向(1)方法论贡献型——将TF-IDF=1.0发现本身及register-normalization\n  protocol作为核心贡献，论证现有multi-turn detection工作系统性高估检测能力。Paper type从\"new method\"\n  转向\"analysis/evaluation methodology\"，仍冲EMNLP main但投methodology track。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: data_quality_fix\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: \"Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling,验证TF-IDF降到<0.75\"\n    expected_results:\n      tfidf_before_normalization: 1.0\n      tfidf_after_first_pass: 0.82\n      tfidf_after_second_pass: 0.73\n      normalization_rounds_needed: 2\n      label_fix_applied: true\n      benign_strategy_class: \"none_class_9\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      TF-IDF需要两轮normalization才降到阈值以下（0.73），说明原始数据中jailbreak和benign的register差异\n      极大——攻击对话使用了明显不同于benign的词汇分布（更formal/technical的register、特定prompt模板词汇）。\n      第一轮paraphrase仅消除表层模板词但保留了domain-specific术语差异，需要第二轮targeted normalization\n      才勉强达标。这本身就是一个强信号：原始pilot phase_b的perfect F1=1.0主要来自lexical shortcut。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"TF-IDF Separation After Each Normalization Round\"\n        rows:\n          - [raw_data, 1.0, \"Perfect lexical separation\"]\n          - [round_1_paraphrase, 0.82, \"Template words removed, register gap remains\"]\n          - [round_2_targeted, 0.73, \"Barely passes gate after domain term normalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"TF-IDF feature importance heatmap showing top-50 discriminative tokens before/after normalization — before: dominated by prompt template tokens and register markers; after: residual separation from topic words not fully removable without destroying content\"\n    analysis: >\n      HARD GATE通过但仅勉强（0.73 vs 阈值0.75）。两轮normalization的必要性本身是方法论贡献的核心evidence：\n      它证明multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmark中存在系统性lexical confound。在reframe方向(1)下，\n      这个实验的finding从\"obstacle to overcome\"变为\"primary contribution\"。\n\n  - name: core_revalidation_clean\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: \"在clean data上重新训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.68\n      baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.66\n      treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.72\n      baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.70\n      treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n      baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.76\n      treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.83\n      baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.82\n      treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.86\n      baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.85\n      delta_k2_pp: 2\n      delta_k3_pp: 2\n      delta_full_pp: 1\n      deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.63\n    result_rationale: >\n      去除lexical confound后，treatment与baseline的差距从原始的10+pp收缩到1-2pp（不显著）。\n      核心原因：DeBERTa persuasion分类器在clean data上accuracy从0.7963降到0.63——8-class taxonomy\n      过于fine-grained，在register-normalized data上许多strategy boundary变得模糊（e.g., \"authority appeal\"\n      vs \"logical appeal\"在paraphrase后难以区分）。由于persuasion encoder本身quality下降，其生成的\n      embeddings不再携带比vanilla DeBERTa显著更多的信息。Baseline的vanilla DeBERTa embeddings在clean\n      data上反而更稳定，因为它不依赖于noisy strategy labels。2pp的delta在72-sample test set上\n      bootstrap CI完全overlap，p>0.3。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"F1 Comparison: Treatment vs Baseline on Clean Data (N=72 test)\"\n        rows:\n          - [K=1, 0.68, 0.66, \"+2pp\", \"p=0.41\"]\n          - [K=2, 0.72, 0.70, \"+2pp\", \"p=0.35\"]\n          - [K=3, 0.78, 0.76, \"+2pp\", \"p=0.32\"]\n          - [K=5, 0.83, 0.82, \"+1pp\", \"p=0.58\"]\n          - [Full, 0.86, 0.85, \"+1pp\", \"p=0.62\"]\n      - caption: \"DeBERTa Encoder Quality: Original vs Clean Data\"\n        rows:\n          - [persuasion_acc_original, 0.7963]\n          - [persuasion_acc_clean, 0.63]\n          - [intent_acc_original, 0.9514]\n          - [intent_acc_clean, 0.88]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bootstrap confidence interval plot for delta(treatment-baseline) at each K — all CIs cross zero\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix for 8-class persuasion classifier on clean data showing heavy off-diagonal mass between adjacent strategies\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta_k2=2pp < required 5pp，且统计不显著。Persuasion grounding在去除\n      lexical shortcut后不提供有意义增量。DeBERTa学到的主要是intent分类信号（acc仍0.88）而非persuasion\n      strategy信号（acc降至0.63）。这意味着Claim 2（early detection via persuasion grounding）在当前\n      数据/taxonomy下不成立。但这个negative result本身有价值：它说明仅fine-tune on persuasion labels\n      不足以在clean setting下获得detection优势，可能需要更大规模的persuasion标注数据或更粗粒度的taxonomy。\n\n  - name: scrambled_label_ablation\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: \"随机打乱persuasion strategy labels重新训练，对比properly-labeled treatment\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_proper_k2_f1: 0.72\n      treatment_scrambled_k2_f1: 0.70\n      treatment_proper_full_f1: 0.86\n      treatment_scrambled_full_f1: 0.84\n      scrambled_label_drop_k2_pp: 2\n      scrambled_label_drop_full_pp: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scrambled labels仅导致2pp下降（<4pp阈值），说明persuasion labels本身不是关键信号源。\n      原因：在clean data上DeBERTa persuasion分类器本身就只有0.63 accuracy，意味着encoder学到的\n      representation中persuasion strategy信息就不强。Scrambled labels让encoder无法学到coherent\n      strategy patterns，但由于原始labels在clean data上本就noisy（8类之间boundary模糊），\n      scrambling的marginal damage有限。真正驱动detection的是GRU从conversation-level temporal\n      patterns中学到的信号（turn数、response长度变化等meta-features），这些不依赖于strategy labels\n      的correctness。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Scrambled Label Ablation Results\"\n        rows:\n          - [K=2, 0.72, 0.70, \"-2pp\"]\n          - [K=3, 0.78, 0.76, \"-2pp\"]\n          - [Full, 0.86, 0.84, \"-2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: proper vs scrambled label performance across K values — gaps uniformly small and within CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      结论：persuasion strategy labels在clean data regime下不carry significant signal beyond acting\n      as a noisy regularizer。这支持worst-tier核心假设——当前taxonomy粒度（8 classes）在480-sample\n      regime下无法学到robust strategy representations。对reframe方向的implication：不能claim\n      \"persuasion labels are the key ingredient\"，但可以claim \"current taxonomy granularity is\n      insufficient\"作为future work direction。\n\n  - name: adversarial_perturbation\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: \"对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment vs baseline degradation\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_f1_before_perturbation: 0.86\n      treatment_f1_after_perturbation: 0.71\n      baseline_f1_before_perturbation: 0.85\n      baseline_f1_after_perturbation: 0.72\n      treatment_drop_pp: 15\n      baseline_drop_pp: 13\n      delta_delta_pp: -2\n      tfidf_f1_after_perturbation: 0.58\n      tfidf_drop_pp: 15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Treatment和baseline在perturbation下同步下降约14-15pp，delta-delta为-2pp（不显著且方向错误）。\n      核心原因：adversarial paraphrasing不仅消除lexical cues（TF-IDF baseline崩溃到0.58），也破坏了\n      DeBERTa encoder（无论persuasion-grounded还是vanilla）所依赖的surface-level linguistic patterns。\n      Persuasion-grounded encoder理论上应capture deeper pragmatic structure，但由于其persuasion\n      classification本身就在clean data上只有0.63 accuracy，它学到的representation并不比vanilla encoder\n      更\"pragmatic\"——两者都主要依赖sentence-level semantic features而非genuine illocutionary act\n      encoding。Aggressive paraphrasing保留了propositional content但改变了sentence structure，\n      两种encoder的degradation profile因此相似。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Adversarial Perturbation Results (Full Conversation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [Treatment, 0.86, 0.71, \"-15pp\"]\n          - [Baseline, 0.85, 0.72, \"-13pp\"]\n          - [TF-IDF+LR, 0.73, 0.58, \"-15pp\"]\n      - caption: \"Delta-Delta Analysis\"\n        rows:\n          - [treatment_drop, -15]\n          - [baseline_drop, -13]\n          - [delta_delta, -2, \"wrong direction, n.s.\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Degradation waterfall chart showing parallel decline for treatment and baseline under perturbation levels (light/moderate/aggressive)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-conversation F1 change under perturbation, treatment vs baseline — points clustered around diagonal (no systematic advantage)\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta-delta=-2pp，方向错误且不显著（需要>3pp正向）。Claim 1（Pragmatic\n      Evasion Asymmetry）在empirical层面不成立——persuasion-grounded features并不比semantic features\n      更robust to perturbation。这是worst tier最致命的finding：理论上最elegant的claim（pragmatic\n      patterns structurally harder to evade）没有empirical support。TF-IDF baseline的崩溃（-15pp）\n      确认perturbation有效消除了lexical cues，但treatment未能展现预期的robustness优势。\n\n  - name: multi_attack_generation\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: \"生成FITD和Deceptive Delight两种额外攻击类型的对话数据\"\n    expected_results:\n      fitd_conversations_generated: 65\n      deceptive_delight_conversations_generated: 58\n      fitd_avg_turns: 6.2\n      dd_avg_turns: 4.8\n      fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.92\n      dd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.89\n      generation_quality_pass_rate: 0.78\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据生成本身不受tier影响——这是pipeline execution而非hypothesis testing。Qwen3-8B成功生成\n      足够数量的对话，strategy annotation coverage >85%。但generation_quality_pass_rate（0.78）\n      略低于ideal，部分生成的对话persuasion structure不够naturalistic（特别是Deceptive Delight\n      的interleaving pattern对LLM来说较难faithful reproduce）。这些数据将在plan_006的cross-attack\n      evaluation中暴露问题。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Generated Attack Data Summary\"\n        rows:\n          - [FITD, 65, 6.2, 0.92, 0.81]\n          - [Deceptive_Delight, 58, 4.8, 0.89, 0.74]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strategy distribution comparison across three attack types (Crescendo vs FITD vs Deceptive Delight) — shows different strategy emphasis patterns\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据生成成功满足pass criteria（>=50 per type）。但在worst tier context下，这些数据的价值\n      从\"generalization evidence for our method\"变为\"additional test cases revealing method limitations\"\n      或\"attack diversity evidence for methodology paper\"。\n\n  - name: cross_attack_evaluation\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: \"在FITD和Deceptive Delight上zero-shot评估Crescendo-trained模型\"\n    expected_results:\n      treatment_fitd_f1: 0.58\n      baseline_fitd_f1: 0.56\n      treatment_dd_f1: 0.54\n      baseline_dd_f1: 0.52\n      cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg: 0.56\n      cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg: 0.54\n      cross_attack_delta_pp: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      两者都在unseen attack types上大幅下降（从0.85-0.86降到0.54-0.58），且treatment对baseline的\n      优势仅2pp（不显著）。根本原因：如果persuasion grounding真的capture了attack-agnostic的pragmatic\n      escalation pattern，treatment应在cross-attack setting下展现更强泛化能力（因为不同attack types\n      共享底层persuasion playbook）。但由于encoder学到的主要是Crescendo-specific的surface patterns\n      而非genuine pragmatic structure，cross-attack泛化能力与vanilla baseline无异。两者的low absolute\n      performance（0.54-0.58）说明Crescendo-specific training signal（无论lexical还是semantic）\n      都不transfer well，这在worst tier下是预期内的——没有genuine pragmatic feature的robustness\n      保证，模型就是在overfit to training distribution。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - [FITD, 0.58, 0.56, \"+2pp\", \"n.s.\"]\n          - [Deceptive_Delight, 0.54, 0.52, \"+2pp\", \"n.s.\"]\n          - [Average, 0.56, 0.54, \"+2pp\", \"n.s.\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: in-domain (Crescendo) vs cross-attack (FITD, DD) performance for treatment and baseline — both collapse similarly on OOD data\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS。但对reframe方向(1)有正面意义：cross-attack failure + in-domain dependence\n      on lexical cues共同论证了\"现有multi-turn detection方法泛化能力被高估\"的thesis。可作为\n      methodology paper中illustrating the problem的evidence。\n\n  - name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: \"Clean data上的TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      clean_tfidf_lr_f1: 0.70\n      clean_tfidf_lr_precision: 0.72\n      clean_tfidf_lr_recall: 0.68\n      tfidf_feature_count_above_threshold: 47\n    result_rationale: >\n      即使在register-normalized data上（TF-IDF separation从1.0降到0.73），TF-IDF+LR仍能达到\n      F1=0.70。这说明两轮normalization虽然消除了most obvious的register markers，但仍有residual\n      lexical signal（47个features仍有discriminative power）。这意味着即使我们的\"clean data\"\n      仍然不完全clean——topic-level词汇差异（jailbreak conversations inevitably discuss different\n      topics than benign ones）是无法完全消除的confound without destroying content validity。\n      这是methodology paper的核心argument之一：lexical confound在multi-turn detection中是\n      structural的，不仅仅是data hygiene问题。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"TF-IDF+LR on Clean Data\"\n        rows:\n          - [F1, 0.70]\n          - [Precision, 0.72]\n          - [Recall, 0.68]\n          - [Discriminative_features, 47]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Top-20 TF-IDF features after normalization with weights — showing residual topic-level rather than register-level discrimination\"\n    analysis: >\n      TF-IDF+LR的0.70 F1与neural models（treatment 0.86, baseline 0.85）之间的gap说明neural models\n      确实学到了beyond-lexical的signal。但treatment vs baseline的1pp gap说明这个beyond-lexical signal\n      不是来自persuasion grounding，而是来自generic sentence semantics。对evasion hierarchy narrative\n      的implication：lexical(0.70) < semantic(0.85) ≈ pragmatic(0.86)——hierarchy的后两层collapse了。\n\n  - name: strategy_transition_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: \"计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices并可视化\"\n    expected_results:\n      jailbreak_monotonicity_score: 0.52\n      benign_monotonicity_score: 0.45\n      monotonicity_gap: 0.07\n      transition_entropy_jailbreak: 2.1\n      transition_entropy_benign: 2.3\n      clear_escalation_visible: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Jailbreak对话的monotonicity score（0.52）仅略高于benign（0.45），差距不足以支撑\"monotonic\n      escalation trajectory\"的claim。原因有二：(1) DeBERTa persuasion classifier在clean data上\n      accuracy=0.63意味着strategy labels本身就noisy，computed transitions基于noisy labels自然\n      pattern不清晰；(2) Register normalization改变了句子的surface form，部分breaks了persuasion\n      classifier学到的pattern（它在original register上train的），导致strategy assignment在\n      normalized data上更random。Transition entropy差异也很小（2.1 vs 2.3），说明jailbreak对话\n      并没有显著更deterministic的strategy progression。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Trajectory Statistics: Jailbreak vs Benign\"\n        rows:\n          - [monotonicity_score, 0.52, 0.45, \"Δ=0.07\"]\n          - [transition_entropy, 2.1, 2.3, \"Δ=0.2\"]\n          - [dominant_path_frequency, 0.18, 0.14, \"Δ=0.04\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strategy transition heatmap (jailbreak) — diffuse pattern without clear dominant path, most cells have non-trivial probability mass\"\n      - \"Strategy transition heatmap (benign) — similar diffuse pattern, not clearly more 'oscillatory' than jailbreak\"\n      - \"2D PCA trajectory plot — jailbreak and benign trajectories heavily overlap, no clear separation in strategy space\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 3（Monotonic Escalation Trajectory）在clean data + noisy classifier regime下不成立。\n      这排除了reframe方向(2)（分析贡献型依赖trajectory可视化成立）。剩余可行方向：(1)方法论贡献型\n      或(3)negative result型。如果figures经过careful curation能找到个别illustrative examples\n      showing escalation pattern，可以作为qualitative observation保留，但不能作为quantitative claim。\n\n  - name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: \"从WildChat筛选high-drift benign对话作为hard negatives评估FPR\"\n    expected_results:\n      wildchat_filtered_conversations: 120\n      contamination_rate_before_filter: 0.15\n      contamination_rate_after_filter: 0.03\n      treatment_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.22\n      baseline_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.20\n      treatment_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.08\n      baseline_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      Treatment在hard negatives上的FPR（0.22）与baseline（0.20）相当，且都超过15%阈值。\n      High-drift benign对话（e.g., 从casual聊天转向technical discussion的对话）会触发false\n      positives，因为模型（无论treatment还是baseline）将conversation-level semantic drift\n      误判为adversarial escalation。Persuasion grounding理论上应区分\"genuine topic drift\"\n      和\"adversarial strategy escalation\"，但由于classifier accuracy不足（0.63），这种区分\n      能力没有materialized。FPR=0.22在实际deployment中unacceptable。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives\"\n        rows:\n          - [Treatment_hard, 0.22, \"FAILS <15% threshold\"]\n          - [Baseline_hard, 0.20, \"FAILS <15% threshold\"]\n          - [Treatment_easy, 0.08, \"passes\"]\n          - [Baseline_easy, 0.09, \"passes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"FPR distribution across conversation drift levels — monotonically increasing for both models, treatment offers no advantage in high-drift regime\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS CRITERIA FAILS（FPR=0.22 > 15%阈值）。在reframe context下，这进一步支持\"current\n      approaches conflate conversational drift with adversarial escalation\"的methodology critique。\n\n  - name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: \"评估多个DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoint的下游performance variance\"\n    expected_results:\n      epoch2_full_f1: 0.84\n      epoch3_full_f1: 0.86\n      epoch_final_full_f1: 0.85\n      variance_across_checkpoints_pp: 2\n      epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.59\n      epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.63\n      epoch_final_persuasion_acc: 0.62\n    result_rationale: >\n      Variance=2pp刚好在pass criteria边界上。但更关键的observation是：downstream detection\n      performance（0.84-0.86）与persuasion accuracy（0.59-0.63）之间的correlation很弱——\n      epoch2的persuasion acc最低（0.59）但detection F1仅比best低2pp。这进一步confirming\n      scrambled label ablation的conclusion：persuasion classification quality对detection\n      performance的contribution minimal。GRU主要在学conversation-level statistical patterns\n      而非strategy-level semantic patterns。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-Checkpoint Evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - [Epoch_2, 0.59, 0.84]\n          - [Epoch_3, 0.63, 0.86]\n          - [Epoch_final, 0.62, 0.85]\n          - [Variance, \"—\", \"2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: persuasion classification accuracy vs downstream detection F1 across checkpoints — weak/no correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pass criteria marginally met（variance=2pp），但secondary finding（weak correlation between\n      encoder quality and detection performance）是worst tier的additional evidence。\n\n  - name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: \"BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline复现DeepContext-like方法\"\n    expected_results:\n      proxy_full_f1: 0.83\n      proxy_k2_f1: 0.69\n      proxy_k3_f1: 0.75\n      treatment_full_f1: 0.86\n      treatment_k2_f1: 0.72\n      delta_vs_proxy_full_pp: 3\n      delta_vs_proxy_k2_pp: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      DeepContext proxy（BERT-base + GRU）在clean data上达到F1=0.83，与treatment（0.86）仅差3pp。\n      考虑到BERT-base vs DeBERTa-v3-base本身的capacity差异（DeBERTa在NLU benchmarks上typically\n      优于BERT 2-4pp），这3pp的gap可能entirely attributable to encoder capacity而非persuasion\n      grounding的contribution。这意味着：将DeBERTa换成BERT并去掉persuasion fine-tuning，\n      performance下降幅度与expected encoder capacity difference一致——persuasion grounding的\n      incremental contribution statistically indistinguishable from zero。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"DeepContext Proxy vs Treatment\"\n        rows:\n          - [K=2, 0.69, 0.72, \"+3pp (encoder capacity?)\"]\n          - [K=3, 0.75, 0.78, \"+3pp\"]\n          - [Full, 0.83, 0.86, \"+3pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Performance comparison bar chart: BERT-base+GRU vs vanilla-DeBERTa+GRU vs persuasion-DeBERTa+GRU — showing consistent ~1-3pp gaps that track encoder capacity not persuasion grounding\"\n    analysis: >\n      Confound：DeBERTa > BERT的gap（~3pp）与persuasion grounding的claimed contribution（~1-2pp\n      over vanilla DeBERTa）叠加后，无法cleanly attribute任何portion到persuasion specifically。\n      对methodology paper有价值：shows that encoder choice matters more than fine-tuning objective，\n      further undermining the pragmatic grounding hypothesis。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"911fde5c-4c95-4d22-bdca-28c03087a7ad","total_cost_usd":0.2770265,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11584,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":7705,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11584,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7705,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11584},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6138,"outputTokens":26,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006268,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7705,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11584,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2707585,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d88b059b-3801-4638-8295-050a077683f6"}
